# ============================================================================
# 06_ Integrate evidence -> ASPC_SIGNATURE + FIBROBLAST_STROMA_SIGNATURE — v6
# ============================================================================
# Final integration step. Consumes the outputs of every upstream script:
#
#   01_ scRNA_batch_pipeline.R (v8)  seurat_merged.rds, cluster.markers.sig_Unknown.csv
#   02_ calculate_tau.R        (v3)  tau_<group>_all_datasets.csv
#   03_ target_cluster_markers (v2)  ratio_<group>_all_datasets.csv,
#                                    target_markers_<group>_recurrence.csv
#   04_ multitask_elasticnet   (v2)  multi_task_coefficients.csv,
#                                    stability_selection.csv
#   05_ wgcna                  (v2)  wgcna_module_membership.csv
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CHANGE IN v6 — TARGET-SIZE SIGNATURE SELECTION
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The v5 run produced ASPC_SIGNATURE = 23 genes and
# FIBROBLAST_STROMA_SIGNATURE = 0 genes. Both are unusable: 23 is too small
# for a stable bulk score, and 0 means the ASPC-down branch is undefined.
#
# The cause is a stack of independent hard gates applied simultaneously:
#     high_tau (tau >= 0.95)      HARD FILTER, applied first
#   + evidence_score >= 1.0
#   + non-NA cor_NEPC and cor_AR
#   + directional correlation gates
#   + ratio_mean >= 1.5
# Each is individually defensible; their intersection is not. tau >= 0.95 in
# particular is near-unreachable for cohorts that 01_ clustered into only 2-3
# groups, because tau's denominator is (n_clusters - 1) — a 2-cluster cohort
# can only produce tau = 1 - min/max, a different quantity entirely.
#
# v6 replaces "filter until whatever survives" with "rank, then take the top
# N", which is how a signature of a specified size should be built:
#
#   * cfg$target_size (default 200) sets the intended signature length.
#   * cfg$selection_mode:
#       "adaptive"  (DEFAULT) walk a relaxation ladder from the strict v5
#                   thresholds downward, stopping at the FIRST tier that
#                   yields >= target_size genes, then rank within that tier
#                   and take the top N. Never relaxes further than needed.
#       "rank_only" apply only the minimum sanity gates, rank, take top N.
#       "strict"    exact v5 behaviour, for reproducing the 23/0 result.
#   * cfg$tau_floor / cfg$ratio_floor bound how far relaxation may go, so the
#     ladder cannot silently descend into meaninglessness.
#   * The tier actually used, and the effective thresholds, are printed and
#     written to signature_selection_diagnostics.csv. Nothing is relaxed
#     invisibly.
#   * cfg$min_marker_cohorts lowered 2 -> 1. With 18 cohorts split across two
#     groups and several clustered coarsely, requiring recurrence in >= 2
#     cohorts caps the candidate pool below the target before any gate runs.
#     The pool size is now reported first, since no amount of threshold
#     relaxation can exceed it.
#
# Ranking within a tier is by: evidence_score, then branch ratio, then tau,
# then |partial_corr|. The gates decide ELIGIBILITY; the ranking decides
# MEMBERSHIP.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# READ THE DIAGNOSTICS, NOT JUST THE GENE LISTS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Relaxing a threshold to reach a target size is target-fitting. It is
# legitimate here ONLY because the ranking is evidence-based and the achieved
# thresholds are recorded. If the run reports that it reached 200 genes only
# at tau >= 0.50, the honest description is "top 200 by evidence among genes
# with tau >= 0.50", not "genes with high cell-type specificity".
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FIXES CARRIED FORWARD
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# v5 — top-level `if (...) expr` NEWLINE `else` is a syntax error; braced.
#      Also added a WGCNA module-size QC gate.
# v4 — namespace masking: select() resolved to MASS::select() because MASS is
#      attached via WGCNA. All dplyr verbs namespace-qualified; stats::cor and
#      stats::sd qualified because WGCNA overrides both.
# v3 — tau column located by candidate-name search, not positional renaming.
# v2 BUG 1 — multi_task_positive / stability_selected were hard-coded FALSE,
#      so 4.5 of ~15 evidence points (the whole ML arm) were inert.
# v2 BUG 2 — v1 residualised on a covariate set INCLUDING ASPC_fraction, then
#      correlated the residual WITH ASPC_fraction: ~0 by construction.
# v2 BUG 3 — `tau` collided on join; ASPC-down branch tested NEPC tau.
# v2 BUG 4 — stale paths. v2 BUG 5 — %||% undefined.
# v2 BUG 6 — in_wgcna_module meant "any non-grey module".
# ============================================================================

